{title: 533 - O for a Faith}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[G]O, for [D7]afaith [G/D]that will not [D]shrink,
[G]Though pressed by [D/F#]many a foe,
[G]That [Em]will not [Am]tremble [D7]on [G]the brink of [D]poverty,
[G]Of poverty or woe; [C]Of poverty [D7]or [G]woe;

Verse 2:
[G]That will [D7]not [G]murmur or complain
[G]Beneath the [D/F#]chastening rod,
[G]But [Em]in the [Am]hour [D7]of grief [G]or pain, of [D]grief [D7]or pain
[G]Can lean upon its God; [C]Can lean upon [D7]its [G]God.

Verse 3:
[G]A faith [D7]that [G]shines more bright [D]and clear
[G]When tempests [Em]rage [D]without;
[G]That [Em]when in [Am]danger [D7]knows [G]no fear, knows [D]of [D7]no fear,
[G]In darkness feels no doubt; [C]In darkness [G/D]feels [D7]no [G]doubt.

Verse 4:
[G]That bears [D7]unmoved [G/D]the world's dread [D]frown,
[G]Nor heeds its [D/F#]scornful smile;
[G]That [Em]sin's wild [Am]ocean [D7]cannot [G]drown, no, [D]cannot [D7]drown,
[G]Nor its soft arts beguile; [C]Nor its soft [G/D]arts beguile.

Verse 5:
[G]Lord, give [D7]me [G]such a faith as [D]this,
[G]And then, [D/F#]whate'er may come
[G]I'll [Em]taste, e'en [Am]here [D7]the hallowed [G]bliss, the [D]hallowed [D7]bliss
[G]Of an eternal home; [C]Of an eternal [G]home.
